    "section": "Ordering Schematic FB5C (3A) and FB5CHT (High Temp)"
  },
  "note": "Extracted by hand from the two schematics on one sheet, folded into one grammar: the FB5C 3A form prints the hard seats alone and the FB5CHT high temp form, not 3A, the full seat ladder. The high temp ladder prints the character B twice, first at the 3.0 hard seat and again at the 3.0 PEEK seat, so the first printing is carried and choosing B raises a caution, the 4700 precedent; the 3.0 PEEK row is left uncoded. The body pairs a finish letter with a Cv letter and the range pairs the standard screw with a range letter, one ZZ across each pair. The TY o-ring and EPDM diaphragm keep their printed size brackets. The body Cv letters are matched to the trim rows as an inferred coupling.",
